{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Fnz9Z7PMf9hyRVSAZ6wJWS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EFJd79LtNJdZgUTNBL4aEW","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\nYour focus areas: **Methods** and **Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\nTitle: \"Progress Stagnation Detection in LLM Agents via Weak Supervision: Gold-Validated Structural and Semantic Approaches\"\n\nThe paper studies progress stagnation detection in LLM coding agents — identifying windows where agents execute seemingly reasonable but collectively ineffective action sequences. Using a weak supervision pipeline with three labeling functions (LFs) over SWE-bench trajectories from SWE-Agent and OpenHands, they compare structural features, neural probes, and LLM-as-judge baselines. A 650-window human gold annotation (κ=0.78) reveals:\n\n1. Structural features achieve 0.89 macro-F1 on gold, outperforming GRU probe (0.84, +5pp) in zero-data deployment, but the gap narrows from 9pp under LF-derived eval — quantifying 10.5pp circular inflation.\n2. The probe shows greater robustness to label noise (−6.5pp LF-to-gold drop vs. −10.5pp for structural). Feature overlap ablation shows non-circular structural features (0.80) underperform the probe (0.84).\n3. Gold disagreement analysis: 79% of MV-gold disagreements are semantically diverse stagnation that structural LFs cannot detect.\n4. Cross-agent transfer: 0.93 F1 after instance isolation (−3.7pp), ~20pp gold-estimated advantage over zero-shot probes.\n5. LLM-as-judge: 5-shot+CoT reaches 0.76 gold F1 at $14.50 and 2800ms/window vs near-zero for structural.\n\n## Key Tables\n- Table 1: Method comparison (LF F1 vs Gold F1): MV 1.000→0.92, Structural GB 0.995→0.89, RF 0.995→0.88, GRU Probe 0.906→0.84, TWV Probe 0.949→0.83, LLM 5-shot 0.76, LLM 0-shot 0.663→0.68\n- Table 2: Gold-MV disagreement: 72 MV=Prog/Gold=Stag (79%), 19 MV=Stag/Gold=Prog (21%). Str 22%/37%, Probe 38%/32%, LLM 52%/42%\n- Table 3: LLM variants cost comparison\n- Table 4: Feature overlap ablation: Full 30dim 0.995→0.89, Non-circular 18dim 0.92→0.80, Probe 0.906→0.84\n- Table 5: Cross-agent instance isolation: Original GB 0.967, Isolated 0.93 (−3.7pp), Probe zero-shot 0.598\n- Table 6 (Appendix A): Gold-MV confusion matrix\n- Table 7 (Appendix B): Claim revision summary\n- Appendix C: Top 5 non-circular features\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\n\nThe planned experiments include:\n1. **gold-set**: 650 windows human gold annotation — all methods re-evaluated. Expected: gold κ=0.78, MV-gold agreement 86%, structural GB gold F1=0.89, probe gold F1=0.84, LLM zero-shot gold F1=0.68.\n2. **llm-judge-fewshot**: LLM-as-judge few-shot + CoT (Claude Sonnet, 5-shot). Expected: gold F1=0.76, +8pp over zero-shot, structural still +13pp ahead, cost $14.50.\n3. **structural-feature-overlap-ablation**: Remove 12 LF-overlapping features, retain 18. Expected: residual gold F1=0.80, below probe 0.84.\n4. **cross-agent-instance-isolation**: Ensure SWE-bench instance isolation between train/test. Expected: GB drops from 0.967 to 0.93 (−3.7pp).\n\n## Your Task\n\nProvide a detailed review covering:\n\n1. **Methodological Soundness** (score 1-5):\n   - Is the problem formulation well-defined?\n   - Are the three detection approaches (structural, probe, LLM) well-motivated and fairly compared?\n   - Is the weak supervision pipeline sound? Are 3 LFs sufficient?\n   - Is the gold annotation protocol adequate (κ=0.78, N=650)?\n   - Is the \"circular evaluation\" analysis convincing?\n\n2. **Experimental Rigor** (score 1-5):\n   - Are the experiments comprehensive enough?\n   - Is the feature overlap ablation well-designed?\n   - Is the instance isolation experiment adequate?\n   - Are statistical significance tests or confidence intervals reported?\n   - Are there missing baselines or ablations?\n   - Does the paper cover all planned experiments from the design?\n\n3. **Clarity of Presentation** (score 1-5)\n\n4. **Strengths** (bullet list)\n\n5. **Weaknesses** (bullet list)\n\n6. **Questions for Authors** (numbered list)\n\n7. **Minor Issues** (bullet list)\n\n8. **Overall Score** (1-6) and **Confidence** (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. Flag genuine issues but acknowledge genuine contributions.","model":"opus"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28537,"cache_read_input_tokens":23530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28537},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b47ecc9-15a3-49db-b5e0-220a3eb8fe8c","uuid":"bf093e35-cfa1-467f-8032-26404c104ae6"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"aa5d5081f835f9637","tool_use_id":"toolu_01EFJd79LtNJdZgUTNBL4aEW","description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review (acceptance rate ~25%, 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept).\n\nYour focus areas: **Methods** and **Experiments**.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\nTitle: \"Progress Stagnation Detection in LLM Agents via Weak Supervision: Gold-Validated Structural and Semantic Approaches\"\n\nThe paper studies progress stagnation detection in LLM coding agents — identifying windows where agents execute seemingly reasonable but collectively ineffective action sequences. Using a weak supervision pipeline with three labeling functions (LFs) over SWE-bench trajectories from SWE-Agent and OpenHands, they compare structural features, neural probes, and LLM-as-judge baselines. A 650-window human gold annotation (κ=0.78) reveals:\n\n1. Structural features achieve 0.89 macro-F1 on gold, outperforming GRU probe (0.84, +5pp) in zero-data deployment, but the gap narrows from 9pp under LF-derived eval — quantifying 10.5pp circular inflation.\n2. The probe shows greater robustness to label noise (−6.5pp LF-to-gold drop vs. −10.5pp for structural). Feature overlap ablation shows non-circular structural features (0.80) underperform the probe (0.84).\n3. Gold disagreement analysis: 79% of MV-gold disagreements are semantically diverse stagnation that structural LFs cannot detect.\n4. Cross-agent transfer: 0.93 F1 after instance isolation (−3.7pp), ~20pp gold-estimated advantage over zero-shot probes.\n5. LLM-as-judge: 5-shot+CoT reaches 0.76 gold F1 at $14.50 and 2800ms/window vs near-zero for structural.\n\n## Key Tables\n- Table 1: Method comparison (LF F1 vs Gold F1): MV 1.000→0.92, Structural GB 0.995→0.89, RF 0.995→0.88, GRU Probe 0.906→0.84, TWV Probe 0.949→0.83, LLM 5-shot 0.76, LLM 0-shot 0.663→0.68\n- Table 2: Gold-MV disagreement: 72 MV=Prog/Gold=Stag (79%), 19 MV=Stag/Gold=Prog (21%). Str 22%/37%, Probe 38%/32%, LLM 52%/42%\n- Table 3: LLM variants cost comparison\n- Table 4: Feature overlap ablation: Full 30dim 0.995→0.89, Non-circular 18dim 0.92→0.80, Probe 0.906→0.84\n- Table 5: Cross-agent instance isolation: Original GB 0.967, Isolated 0.93 (−3.7pp), Probe zero-shot 0.598\n- Table 6 (Appendix A): Gold-MV confusion matrix\n- Table 7 (Appendix B): Claim revision summary\n- Appendix C: Top 5 non-circular features\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\n\nThe planned experiments include:\n1. **gold-set**: 650 windows human gold annotation — all methods re-evaluated. Expected: gold κ=0.78, MV-gold agreement 86%, structural GB gold F1=0.89, probe gold F1=0.84, LLM zero-shot gold F1=0.68.\n2. **llm-judge-fewshot**: LLM-as-judge few-shot + CoT (Claude Sonnet, 5-shot). Expected: gold F1=0.76, +8pp over zero-shot, structural still +13pp ahead, cost $14.50.\n3. **structural-feature-overlap-ablation**: Remove 12 LF-overlapping features, retain 18. Expected: residual gold F1=0.80, below probe 0.84.\n4. **cross-agent-instance-isolation**: Ensure SWE-bench instance isolation between train/test. Expected: GB drops from 0.967 to 0.93 (−3.7pp).\n\n## Your Task\n\nProvide a detailed review covering:\n\n1. **Methodological Soundness** (score 1-5):\n   - Is the problem formulation well-defined?\n   - Are the three detection approaches (structural, probe, LLM) well-motivated and fairly compared?\n   - Is the weak supervision pipeline sound? Are 3 LFs sufficient?\n   - Is the gold annotation protocol adequate (κ=0.78, N=650)?\n   - Is the \"circular evaluation\" analysis convincing?\n\n2. **Experimental Rigor** (score 1-5):\n   - Are the experiments comprehensive enough?\n   - Is the feature overlap ablation well-designed?\n   - Is the instance isolation experiment adequate?\n   - Are statistical significance tests or confidence intervals reported?\n   - Are there missing baselines or ablations?\n   - Does the paper cover all planned experiments from the design?\n\n3. **Clarity of Presentation** (score 1-5)\n\n4. **Strengths** (bullet list)\n\n5. **Weaknesses** (bullet list)\n\n6. **Questions for Authors** (numbered list)\n\n7. **Minor Issues** (bullet list)\n\n8. **Overall Score** (1-6) and **Confidence** (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. Flag genuine issues but acknowledge genuine contributions.","uuid":"618d61cc-859d-46c0-9049-1e536cfc5a72","session_id":"5b47ecc9-15a3-49db-b5e0-220a3eb8fe8c"}
