%/42%\n- Table 3: LLM variants cost comparison\n- Table 4: Feature overlap ablation: Full 30dim 0.995→0.89, Non-circular 18dim 0.92→0.80, Probe 0.906→0.84\n- Table 5: Cross-agent instance isolation: Original GB 0.967, Isolated 0.93 (−3.7pp), Probe zero-shot 0.598\n- Table 6 (Appendix A): Gold-MV confusion matrix\n- Table 7 (Appendix B): Claim revision summary\n- Appendix C: Top 5 non-circular features\n\n## Experiment Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\n\nThe planned experiments include:\n1. **gold-set**: 650 windows human gold annotation — all methods re-evaluated. Expected: gold κ=0.78, MV-gold agreement 86%, structural GB gold F1=0.89, probe gold F1=0.84, LLM zero-shot gold F1=0.68.\n2. **llm-judge-fewshot**: LLM-as-judge few-shot + CoT (Claude Sonnet, 5-shot). Expected: gold F1=0.76, +8pp over zero-shot, structural still +13pp ahead, cost $14.50.\n3. **structural-feature-overlap-ablation**: Remove 12 LF-overlapping features, retain 18. Expected: residual gold F1=0.80, below probe 0.84.\n4. **cross-agent-instance-isolation**: Ensure SWE-bench instance isolation between train/test. Expected: GB drops from 0.967 to 0.93 (−3.7pp).\n\n## Your Task\n\nProvide a detailed review covering:\n\n1. **Methodological Soundness** (score 1-5):\n   - Is the problem formulation well-defined?\n   - Are the three detection approaches (structural, probe, LLM) well-motivated and fairly compared?\n   - Is the weak supervision pipeline sound? Are 3 LFs sufficient?\n   - Is the gold annotation protocol adequate (κ=0.78, N=650)?\n   - Is the \"circular evaluation\" analysis convincing?\n\n2. **Experimental Rigor** (score 1-5):\n   - Are the experiments comprehensive enough?\n   - Is the feature overlap ablation well-designed?\n   - Is the instance isolation experiment adequate?\n   - Are statistical significance tests or confidence intervals reported?\n   - Are there missing baselines or ablations?\n   - Does the paper cover all planned experiments from the design?\n\n3. **Clarity of Presentation** (score 1-5)\n\n4. **Strengths** (bullet list)\n\n5. **Weaknesses** (bullet list)\n\n6. **Questions for Authors** (numbered list)\n\n7. **Minor Issues** (bullet list)\n\n8. **Overall Score** (1-6) and **Confidence** (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. Flag genuine issues but acknowledge genuine contributions."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EFJd79LtNJdZgUTNBL4aEW","session_id":"5b47ecc9-15a3-49db-b5e0-220a3eb8fe8c","uuid":"b978cb7b-f845-4b42-9058-bd26c3cdc152","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:26:12.062Z"}
