w novel is the gold-validated comparison methodology?\n   - Is there sufficient technical novelty beyond empirical comparison?\n\n2. **Related Work Coverage** (score 1-5):\n   - Are key related works cited and adequately discussed?\n   - Missing citations? (Consider: agent benchmarks like SWE-bench itself, other weak supervision extensions, process supervision, step-level reward models, other agent monitoring systems, runtime guardrails)\n   - Is the positioning against prior work fair and accurate?\n   - Does the paper clearly articulate its contribution relative to existing work?\n\n3. **Significance and Impact** (score 1-5):\n   - How important is this problem?\n   - Are the findings actionable for practitioners?\n   - Will this work influence future research?\n\n4. **Strengths** (bullet list)\n\n5. **Weaknesses** (bullet list)\n\n6. **Questions for Authors** (numbered list)\n\n7. **Missing Related Work** (specific papers/areas the authors should discuss)\n\n8. **Overall Score** (1-6) and **Confidence** (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. Consider both the novelty of the individual components and the overall contribution as a package.","uuid":"01c906b3-f805-4604-a795-e02933986a17","session_id":"5b47ecc9-15a3-49db-b5e0-220a3eb8fe8c"}
