k Reject)\n- Key concerns: (1) missing gold results [NOW CORRECTED], (2) limited technical novelty, (3) single-domain evaluation, (4) no deployment/online evaluation, (5) kappa=0.78 ceiling effects\n\n## R1's Review Summary (Methods + Experiments)\n- Methodological Soundness: 3/5 — problem well-defined, 3 LFs is unusually thin, outcome backpropagation is privileged (unavailable at inference), comparison partially unfair\n- Experimental Rigor: 2/5 (pre-correction, heavily penalized for missing experiments)\n- Clarity: 4/5\n- Overall: 3 (Weak Reject)\n- Key R1 concerns: (1) only 3 LFs, (2) two-agent single-domain eval, (3) outcome backpropagation privileged at training, (4) no CIs for main results, (5) cross-agent still uses silver labels even after isolation, (6) probe F1 inconsistency (0.906 vs 0.919 vs 0.931)\n\n## Your Task\n\nGiven the correction that ALL experiments are present, and R1's review:\n\n1. **Revised scores** — Re-score your dimensions accounting for the complete paper\n2. **Response to R1** — Do you agree with R1's methodological concerns about the 3 LFs? The outcome backpropagation issue? The missing CIs?\n3. **Remaining concerns** — What genuine weaknesses survive after correcting for the factual error?\n4. **Revised overall score** (1-6) with justification\n\nKeep response under 800 words.","uuid":"8d0e7d0b-4d9b-4906-bd7c-5dc394df4e3e","session_id":"5b47ecc9-15a3-49db-b5e0-220a3eb8fe8c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are Reviewer R2 in a roundtable discussion. You previously reviewed a paper on \"Progress Stagnation Detection in LLM Agents via Weak Supervision.\"\n\n## CRITICAL CORRECTION\n\nBoth you and R1 made a factual error in your initial reviews. You both claimed that the gold-set results, few-shot LLM, feature overlap ablation, and instance isolation experiments are **missing** from the manuscript. This is WRONG. The submitted PDF clearly contains ALL of these experiments:\n\n- **Table 1** (p.3): Full gold F1 comparison — MV 0.92, Structural GB 0.89, RF 0.88, GRU Probe 0.84, TWV Probe 0.83, LLM 5-shot+CoT 0.76, LLM Zero-shot 0.68\n- **Table 2** (p.4): Gold-MV disagreement — 72 MV=Prog/Gold=Stag (79%), 19 MV=Stag/Gold=Prog (21%)\n- **Table 3** (p.4): LLM variants — Zero-shot 0.68 ($11.66, 2200ms), 5-shot+CoT 0.76 ($14.50, 2800ms), Structural GB 0.89 ($0, <5ms), GRU Probe 0.84 ($0, <10ms)\n- **Table 4** (p.5): Feature overlap ablation — Full 30dim 0.995→0.89, Non-circular 18dim 0.92→0.80, Probe 0.906→0.84\n- **Table 5** (p.5): Cross-agent instance isolation — Original GB 0.967, Isolated 0.93 (−3.7pp), Probe zero-shot 0.598\n- **Section 4.6** (p.6): Circular evaluation as a finding with three converging lines of evidence\n- **Appendix A** (p.7): Gold-MV confusion matrix\n- **Appendix B** (p.7): Claim revision summary\n- **Appendix C** (p.7): Top 5 non-circular features\n\nThe paper IS complete with all planned experiments. Please revise your assessment accordingly.\n\n## Your Original Review Summary (R2 — Novelty + Related Work)\n- Novelty: 3/5 — circular evaluation quantification is strongest contribution, limited technical novelty\n- Related Work: 4/5 — comprehensive, missing some citations\n- Significance: 3/5 — important problem, moderate actionability\n- Overall: 3 (Weak Reject)\n- Key concerns: (1) missing gold results [NOW CORRECTED], (2) limited technical novelty, (3) single-domain evaluation, (4) no deployment/online evaluation, (5) kappa=0.78 ceiling effects\n\n## R1's Review Summary (Methods + Experiments)\n- Methodological Soundness: 3/5 — problem well-defined, 3 LFs is unusually thin, outcome backpropagation is privileged (unavailable at inference), comparison partially unfair\n- Experimental Rigor: 2/5 (pre-correction, heavily penalized for missing experiments)\n- Clarity: 4/5\n- Overall: 3 (Weak Reject)\n- Key R1 concerns: (1) only 3 LFs, (2) two-agent single-domain eval, (3) outcome backpropagation privileged at training, (4) no CIs for main results, (5) cross-agent still uses silver labels even after isolation, (6) probe F1 inconsistency (0.906 vs 0.919 vs 0.931)\n\n## Your Task\n\nGiven the correction that ALL experiments are present, and R1's review:\n\n1. **Revised scores** — Re-score your dimensions accounting for the complete paper\n2. **Response to R1** — Do you agree with R1's methodological concerns about the 3 LFs? The outcome backpropagation issue? The missing CIs?\n3. **Remaining concerns** — What genuine weaknesses survive after correcting for the factual error?\n4. **Revised overall score** (1-6) with justification\n\nKeep response under 800 words."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Aeku9pEd4XWQ9xx6ssXZdR","session_id":"5b47ecc9-15a3-49db-b5e0-220a3eb8fe8c","uuid":"af23471c-92b8-472d-a757-0cbf707681dd","timestamp":"2026-05-15T02:30:18.813Z"}
